      "id": "claim_24f0eefd4ee244179e9975119dc3cfb8",
      "statement": "The non-negotiable core principles are: (1) zero telemetry (upstream OTEL/OTLP surfaces skipped, not deferred; OTEL_* env vars inert; config schema omits experimental.openTelemetry), (2) reference-not-contract (legacy REST/SSE mirrored for verifiability; deviations only on explicit user instruction and logged; standing x-yolo-directory deviation), (3) pins are change gates not upstream locks (sha256 pins re-baselined in the same commit, never left dangling), (4) TUI is a pure client (enforced by TestImportsDirection), (5) tests define the contract, (6) task state in beads and proven knowledge in docs, (7) subagents one at a time, (8) YOLO spawns only YOLO.",
